## 9. Linting & Code Quality

- Use the project linter/formatter when present
- No dead code, no commented-out blocks
- Functions short; avoid nesting > 2 levels (prefer early return)
- One responsibility per function/class; prefer pure functions in `domain`
- No silent failures; use explicit domain exceptions (`CurrencyMismatchException`,
  `InvalidJournalEntryException`, etc.), never a swallowed exception
- No unused dependencies; justify new deps in `docs/PLAN_LEDGER_FINTECH.md` or an ADR,
  and confirm they don't violate the non-presumption principle (should they be optional
  and behind a port, not a hard dependency of the core?)
- Same patterns across the codebase — a new adapter follows the shape of an existing one

### Self-check before finishing a task

- Layers respected? (`domain` still zero-framework?) If not → FIX
- Business logic outside `domain`/`application`? → FIX
- Pricing/fee calculation leaking into core? → FIX (port + optional adapter)
- A vendor SDK type leaking into a port signature? → FIX (extract an abstraction)
- Over-engineered relative to what §2.3's extension table actually needs? → SIMPLIFY
- Understandable in <30s? → SIMPLIFY
- Domain invariants (append-only, sum-zero, idempotency) still enforced and tested? →
  ADD tests if missing
- Tests pass locally (`mvn verify`)? If not → FIX before committing

